{
  "_comment": [
    "What tenant id each YAML spelling of a `tenants:` key IS (#2114).",
    "`source` is the key exactly as written in the file (quotes included);",
    "each row is decoded from `tenants:\\n  <source>:\\n    mysql_connections: \"1\"\\n`.",
    "`exporter_key` is the key the exporter's decode yields (null = no tenant:",
    "the key is dropped). Go (components/threshold-exporter/app/pkg/config/",
    "tenant_id_spelling_parity_test.go) decodes each row through",
    "config.ParseConfigFile, the flat plane's own decode, and asserts this column;",
    "Python (tests/shared/test_tenant_id_yaml_spelling_parity.py) asserts that",
    "_lib_yaml_keys reads the same key. Neither reads the other's source.",
    "`safe_load_str` is str() of the key yaml.safe_load (YAML 1.1 typing) gives —",
    "what the Python tools used as the tenant id before #2114. Only the Python",
    "half asserts it; it is kept so the table shows which rows the old read got",
    "wrong (13 of 22), i.e. that the table can tell the two readers apart."
  ],
  "spellings": [
